C('8-028',[58,59],'J156-8-08','5-43','Y′=∅, X′≠∅','Inverse image along a non-surjective map, when viewed on elementary strata and allowing a zero image, need not preserve face incidence: an ambient stratum can have empty interior inverse image while one boundary face survives. It therefore falls outside the current strong magasin homomorphism definition. Multiplication by a fixed nonempty figure and product F↦F×F′ can also send an elementary figure to a composite figure.','proof sketched','morphisms')
C('8-029',[60,61,62,63],'J156-8-08','47-101','Alors M′ ... est un magasin','A subset M′ closed under taking faces, equipped with induced primitive relations, is asserted to inherit the magasin structure and the derived relations; the text also imposes closure under carriers X≪°Y′≤Y when X,Y∈M′. Under literal face closure this carrier clause is redundant. The corresponding subatlas consists of figures whose strata belong to M′ and preserves arbitrary existing joins/nonempty meets. Additional local/divisibility assertions assume M′ contains all lieux; open-refinement closure suffices for preserving the absence-of-common-refinement disjointness description.','proof sketched','morphisms')
C('8-030',[64,65,66],'J156-8-08','126-168','commute aux Sup ... (**)... isom.','A join-preserving atlas map is determined by values on elementary figures; binary meet preservation is the face formula f(X)∩f(Y)=sup_{Z≤X,Y}f(Z). Preserving arbitrary nonempty meets additionally involves decreasing filtered families. Requiring Sub(F)≅Sub(f(F)) forces elementary figures to map to elementary figures, recovering the stronger face-bijective definition. The claim that any monotone elementary-value map extends under finiteness/unconditionality omits compatibility of its values and must not be accepted without that hypothesis.','stated without proof','order')
C('8-031',[66,67],'J156-8-09','8-35','Si c’est injectif ... pas automatique je présume','A face-bijective magasin homomorphism need not be globally injective. Even when injective, reflection of refinement and disjointness is not proved; if refinement is reflected, carrier uniqueness shows the image is carrier-closed and open refinement is reflected. Additional reflection hypotheses for the other relations remain discussed rather than established.','open on the pages','morphisms')
C('8-032',[67,68,69,70,71],'J156-8-09','41-198','Théorème ... fonctions support externe','Strong magasin homomorphisms M→Figel(P), with principal face-set bijections, correspond to maps X↦|X|⊆P satisfying: X≪Y⇒|X|⊆|Y|; X⟂°Y⇒|X|°∩|Y|°=∅; every |X|° nonempty; and |X|=⋃_{Y≤X}|Y|°. The homomorphism is X↦{|Y|:Y≤X}. Normalization restricts P to the total support then identifies points with equal membership profiles. Faithfulness additionally reflects disjointness, and a set realization also reflects both orders.','proved there','support')
C('8-033',[71,72,73],'J156-8-09','198-230','2.7. C’est inexact ... pas fidèle','The initial assertion that all examples examined admit natural faithful external supports is corrected on 2 July: for topological pseudosegments/cordes/ficelles, the natural support is not generally faithful. Scan73 Example2 retains the earlier contrary assertion and is governed by this correction. The tautological full-shadow support always exists; its faithfulness is equivalent to disjointness being absence of a common open refinement. For a maquette, support ↓X has interior {X} and is faithful.','corrected by himself later (both places)','support')
C('8-034',[74,75,76],'J156-8-10','6-84','cosupp° ... supp° ... antiinvolution','For a symmetric irreflexive relation on M, A⊥={x:∀a∈A,a⊥x} is antitone and A↦A⊥⊥ a closure operator. Its fixed sets form a complete ortholattice: meet=intersection, join=double-perpendicular of union, and perpendicular is an order-reversing involution with bottom ∅ and top M. Magasin supports are also lower for open refinement. These interior supports differ from supports formed from whole-figure disjointness; a deleted equality of the two cosupports is expressly rejected as idiot.','proof sketched','ortholattice')
C('8-035',[77,78],'J156-8-10','86-166','deux applications ... inverses','Under Mog L2, restriction S↦S∩L gives an ortholattice isomorphism Σ_M≅Σ_L; its inverse is A↦A⊥⊥ in M, equivalently {X:omb°X⊆A}. In the quasi-set-theoretic case this gives Σ_M≅P(L). A two-set relational generalization is proposed but its full statement and verification are explicitly deferred.','proof sketched','galois')
C('8-036',[79,80,81],'J156-8-10','173-269','est injective ... Il ne commute pas aux A∩B','A faithful external support induces an order embedding Σ_M→P(P), S↦⋃_{X∈S}|X|°. The hope that it preserve all lattice operations and complements is not justified; the margin supplies a crossing-cell picture where intrinsic supports have empty intersection but realized sets intersect. A left inverse on arbitrary subsets can be formed by double-perpendicular closure of elements whose interiors lie in the subset.','corrected by himself later (both places)','support')
C('8-037',[82,83,84,85],'J156-8-11','16-176','j’aimerais ... C’est trop fort ... Pas tout à fait','For principal supports, equality of the realized double-perpendicular support with |X|° requires a separation property: every point of a competing interior outside |X|° must meet an interior disjoint from X. Several stronger whole-support conditions are proposed then weakened. These are exploratory sufficient conditions; the argument explicitly moves to constructible supports rather than proving the initial unrestricted hope.','open on the pages','support')
C('8-038',[85,86,87,88],'J156-8-11','174-310','pleinement fidèle ... Proposition ... Corollaire 1','Fix an atlas and a faithful external support. Full faithfulness means P∖|F| is the union of interiors of elements interior-disjoint from all strata of each atlas figure F. If Φ⊆F, then the realization of Φ⊥⊥ equals ⋃_{X∈Φ}|X|°. Consequently Φ↦Φ⊥⊥ preserves arbitrary joins, nonempty meets, and relative complements inside one figure; these admissible constructible supports have Boolean/distributive set calculus. The unrestricted claim without full faithfulness is answered No in the margin.','proved there','support')
C('8-039',[88,89],'J156-8-11','314-344','Axiome supp 1','The support axiom is F⊥⊥∩Φ⊥=(F∖Φ)⊥⊥ for every atlas figure F and subset Φ⊆F. Full faithfulness implies it. It only involves incidence and interior disjointness, not open refinement. The author plans disjunctive examples where it fails and marks the possibility Yes; the later disjunctor analysis must govern its status.','proof sketched','ortholattice')
P('8-09','General quotients and maps sending strata to zero or composites',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':58,'file':'J156-8-08','lines':'5-25'},{'cote':'156-8','scan':65,'file':'J156-8-08','lines':'150-168'}],'A general inverse image or product should be accommodated although elementary figures may map to zero or composite figures.','Use partial/relational or support-level morphisms, with explicitly controlled incidence loss; current strong homomorphisms cover only the face-bijective case.')
P('8-10','When is an injective strong morphism an embedding?',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':66,'file':'J156-8-09','lines':'19-27'},{'cote':'156-8','scan':67,'file':'J156-8-09','lines':'32-35'}],'Does injectivity identify M with a submagasin? Refinement reflection is not automatic, it seems.','Distinguish injectivity from reflection of both orders and orthogonality; prove the exact criterion or give a finite counterexample.')
P('8-11','General relational support reduction',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':78,'file':'J156-8-10','lines':'134-160'}],'Write and verify the general two-set version of the support isomorphism.','For a relation induced by a family of nonempty subsets with all singleton generators present, compare the Galois closed-set lattices; formulate density hypotheses explicitly.')
P('8-12','Faithful versus fully faithful external support',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':88,'file':'J156-8-11','lines':'309-312'},{'cote':'156-8','scan':89,'file':'J156-8-11','lines':'335-344'}],'Find a faithful external support that is not fully faithful, and inspect the ordered-set examples.','Fidelity preserves orthogonality but full faithfulness supplies pointwise complement coverage for every allowed figure; compare the two through explicit finite relation models and the support axiom.')
P('8-13','Metric separation examples',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':72,'file':'J156-8-09','lines':'208'}],'Can geometries whose disjointness means distance >ε or ≥ε fit the magasin language? The author has not checked enough to know.','Specify a scale, nonempty regions, admissible refinements, and carrier/disjointness axioms; test a finite metric model before claiming a general metric realization.')
R('156-8',64,'J156-8-08:130','n’importe quelle application croissante extends','Check for an omitted compatibility condition','Two compatible incomparable source strata may map to incompatible target figures; unconditional figures still need compatible unions. The missing condition could be mathematical omission rather than transcription error.')
R('156-8',65,'J156-8-08:158','G↦G′=f(F)','G′=f(G)','A constant map cannot be an isomorphism of nontrivial subfigure posets.')
